# Web UI

Guardrails: G-02, G-04, G-05, G-06, G-07

## Display (G-04, G-05)

- Render Unknown as the word "Unknown", never as 0, a dash that reads as zero, or blank.
- Show coverage and as-of context wherever figures appear; missing coverage is not zero exposure.
- Mark derived values as derived and link reported values to their source.

## Data (G-02, G-07)

- The web layer only formats values it receives. It does not compute financial figures.
- No hard-coded or mock financial numbers, borrower names, or BDC names in components,
  pages, stories, or demos.

## No scores (G-06)

- See `no-scores-rankings.mdc`.

## Framework

- This app uses a recent Next.js with breaking changes. Read `apps/web/AGENTS.md` and the
  bundled docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing framework code.

```tsx
// BAD
<td>{value ?? 0}</td>
// GOOD
<td>{value === null ? "Unknown" : formatAmount(value)}</td>
```
